cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "satprint: Satellite Terrain to 3D-Printable Models"
abstract: >
  satprint turns satellite elevation data into watertight, 3D-printable
  terrain models scaled to the printer, with a solid base. Cities can carry
  their OpenStreetMap buildings as closed solids, and a multi-color 3MF splits
  the model into land, water, buildings and a border frame for multi-material
  printers. A textured GLB drapes satellite imagery over the terrain for
  viewing. It runs as a web app, a command-line tool and a REST API.
